js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0bthp5j0z266g.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0g_miwgby_mg4.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0bgb1-s946o7g.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0rw187uandnvm.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/13twdpqxz8tr6.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0q~nc9msbar7h.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/15lxb7jjl82fj.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0hvb31nnv6dpj.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\"],\"default\"]\n4b:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\""])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Meet strict data privacy requirements\"}],\" - If you’re operating a B2B SaaS platform with customers in regulated industries, they may require maximum data isolation at the instance level. A database-per-tenant approach allows you to meet these stringent data privacy demands by offering each customer their own isolated database.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Comply with regional data regulations\"}],\" - In cases where data regulations require customer data to be stored within specific regions, creating separate databases in each region provides a straightforward path to compliance.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Simplify management\"}],\" - If your customers require isolated workflows like backups, PITR, or migrations, database-per-tenant makes these easier to manage without cross-tenant risk.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Avoiding noisy neighbors\"}],\" - When customers share an instance, a spike in usage from one tenant can degrade performance for others. Isolating tenants ensures consistent performance.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n4c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L74\",null,{\"src\":\"/use-cases/multitenant-postgres-instance-per-tenant.jpg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L75\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg\",\"src\":\"/use-cases/multitenant-postgres-instance-per-tenant.jpg\",\"width\":704,\"height\":447,\"style\":{\"width\":\"100%\",\"height\":\"100%\"},\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"alt\":\"Postgres instance per tenant\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-10 border border-black mix-blend-overlay dark:border-white rounded-lg\",\"aria-hidden\":true}]]}]}]\n4d:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"scaling-database-per-user-architectures-in-aws-is-not-a-good-idea\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Scaling database-per-user architectures in AWS is not a good idea\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#scaling-database-per-user-architectures-in-aws-is-not-a-good-idea\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Scaling database-per-user architectures in AWS is not a good idea\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$3f:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n4e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Managed Postgres services like Amazon RDS weren’t designed for high-volume, database-per-tenant use cases. While you can technically isolate each customer with their own database, doing so at scale becomes operationally and financially unsustainable.\\nThere are two common paths teams take—both with major drawbacks:\"}]\n4f:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"1-cramming-thousands-of-databases-into-a-single-rds-instance\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"1. Cramming thousands of databases into a single RDS instance\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#1-cramming-thousands-of-databases-into-a-single-rds-instance\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to 1. Cramming thousands of databases into a single RDS instance\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$3f:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n50:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Many teams try to save money by putting all their tenants into one large RDS instance"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,". But this leads to:\"}]\n51:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Single point of failure\"}],\" - If that instance goes down, all of your customers are impacted.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Noisy neighbors\"}],\" - Resource-hungry tenants can degrade performance for others sharing the same compute.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Complex maintenance\"}],\" - Backups, PITR, monitoring, and upgrades become harder to manage when they're tied to a massive shared instance.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Rigid scaling\"}],\" - You can’t scale individual tenants—you have to scale the entire instance, often overpaying for idle capacity.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n52:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L74\",null,{\"src\":\"/use-cases/multitenant-single-postgres-instance.jpg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L75\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg\",\"src\":\"/use-cases/multitenant-single-postgres-instance.jpg\",\"width\":704,\"height\":447,\"style\":{\"width\":\"100%\",\"height\":\"100%\"},\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"alt\":\"Multi-tenant Postgres instance for all tenants\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-10 border border-black mix-blend-overlay dark:border-white rounded-lg\",\"aria-hidden\":true}]]}]}]\n53:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"2-spinning-up-one-rds-instance-per-tenant\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"2. Spinning up one RDS instance per tenant\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#2-spinning-up-one-rds-instance-per-tenant\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to 2. Spinning up one RDS instance per tenant\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$3f:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n54:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This approach gives you the isolation you’re looking for, but it comes at a steep cost—both in dollars and engineering time. The truth is, RDS was never designed for this kind of architecture:\"}]\n55:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Expensive and wasteful\"}],\" - Each RDS instance has a baseline cost, even when idle. Multiply that across hundreds or thousands of tenants, and your bill quickly becomes unsustainable. Storage also doesn’t scale down: once it grows, you’re stuck paying for it.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"No dynamic scaling\"}],\" - RDS instances don’t autoscale. Resizing compute often requires manual intervention—and in many cases, downtime.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"High operational burden\"}],\" - You’ll soon need a dedicated team just to handle instance provisioning, monitoring, patching, and scaling logistics. Even basic tasks become complex at scale.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Slow setups\"}],\" - Spinning up a new RDS instance can take minutes, not seconds—far from ideal from the end-user experience.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n56:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"quote my-8 border-l-2 border-green-44 pl-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"blockquote\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[710px] border-none p-0 font-mono text-xl leading-snug font-normal tracking-extra-tight text-black-pure dark:text-white sm:text-lg\",\"children\":[\"\\\"\",\"Our customers require their data to live in an isolated database, but implementing this in RDS was cumbersome and expensive\",\"\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"figcaption\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between gap-2.5\",\"childr"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"en\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2.5\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-base leading-snug tracking-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-me